                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew letter Ayin Stock Vector Image &amp; Art - Alamy](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110524-2762-0139-0000-6276222ddde4:4)\nAyin (**ע** ) is the `16th letter of the Hebrew alphabet` with a numerical value of **70**.[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Ayin/ayin.html)\n\n### Meaning and Symbolism\n\n- **Eye and Sight:** The word *Ayin* literally means \"eye\" or \"to see,\" symbolizing perception, spiritual insight, and divine watchfulness.\n- **Spring or Source:** The same root word (*ma'ayan* ) means a natural spring or fountain of water.\n- **Humility:** In modern and traditional Hebrew, Ayin is largely a silent consonant (functioning as a glottal stop in some traditional pronunciations), representing quiet humility.\n- **Number 70:** Historically and biblically, 70 represents the 70 elders of Israel, the 70 faces of the Torah, and the 70 nations.[[1]](https://hebrewtoday.com/alphabet/the-letter-ain-%D7%A2/)[[2]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Ayin/ayin.html)[[3]](https://dinahoverlien.com/2020/07/22/ayin/)[[4]](https://jhvonline.com/ayin-p14595-288.htm)[[5]](https://inner.org/hebleter/ayin.htm)\n\n### Forms and Pronunciation\n\n- **Block Script:** **ע** \n- **Sound:** Silent in Modern Hebrew, though historically or in Sephardic/Mizrahi traditions it is a deep guttural throat sound.\n- **Origin:** Derived from an ancient pictograph of an eye found in early Semitic scripts (which also evolved into the Latin letter **O**).[[1]](https://jhvonline.com/ayin-p14595-288.htm)[[2]](https://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/2188-ayin)[[3]](https://www.ancient-hebrew.org/ancient-alphabet/ayin.htm)\n\nYou can read more detailed linguistic and mystical insights via [Chabad.org](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137088/jewish/Ayin.htm) or [Hebrew4Christians](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Ayin/ayin.html).[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Ayin/ayin.html)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137088/jewish/Ayin.htm)Would you like to explore **gematria connections** for Ayin, or learn about words that start with this letter?",
